## MAUI

### View Model guidelines

- every view model class should inherit ObservableObject.
- use MVVM Toolkit [ObservableProperty] for source generated property.
- use MVVM Toolkit [RelayCommand] for source generated command.

### XAML guidelines (only `.xaml` files)

- Prefer `VerticalStackLayout` and `HorizontalStackLayout` over `StackLayout`.
- Use `Grid` for structured layout instead of nested stacks.
- Use resource references (`{StaticResource}` or `{DynamicResource}`) instead of hardcoded colors, if possible.
- Avoid inline styles unless specifically required.

### Addiditonal, to be tested

- Use self-closing tags (`<ElementName />`) for elements that have no child content.
- Preserve XML declaration (`<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>`).
- Order elements hierarchically — parent controls first, children below.
- Keep attributes in a consistent order.
- Sort namespace declarations alphabetically by prefix.
- Place one attribute per line if a tag has more than two attributes.
- Align attribute indentation to one level deeper than the element start.
- No trailing spaces.
- Keep one blank line between top-level elements.
- Do not insert blank lines between child elements inside the same container.
- Use PascalCase for control names: `MainGrid`, `SubmitButton`.
- Use camelCase for resource keys: `primaryBrush`, `accentColor`.
- Prefer `{Binding PropertyName}` syntax without `Path=`.
- Use `Content` property implicitly (no explicit `Content="..."` for `Button`, `Label`, etc. if unnecessary).